  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The intended audience is individuals who hold or are influenced by religiously motivated communal tensions, particularly those who believe in or support the idea of blaming Hindus for violence in religion-based riots while absolving minorities from guilt. This audience is likely composed of members of religious minorities (e.g., Muslims, Christians, Sikhs) who may be targeted by such divisive narratives, or those who are politically or ideologically aligned with the 'divide and rule' strategy. The meme targets those who are familiar with or sympathetic to the concept of religious scapegoating and systemic injustice, and who may be seeking or reinforcing a narrative of victimhood for their own community or a perceived enemy group.",
